fix(brand): the social card advertised SCRIPTHAMMER.COM

geolarp.com's Open Graph image was ScriptHammer's logo with
SCRIPTHAMMER.COM rendered into the artwork, twice. Byte-identical to an
upstream blob. Anyone sharing the link on Slack, Discord, Twitter or
Facebook saw that card.

A rebrand substitutes strings and a logo is not a string, so the sweep
cannot reach a .png. Same class as #659 and #898, one layer further out.
Regenerated from the geoLARP mark: die, globe, wordmark, tagline.

Two template strings were wrong for the same reason, carrying no brand
token for the sweep to match:

  metadata.tsx      appended "- Modern Web Starter" to every social title
  project.config    projectDescription still described a Next.js/Supabase
                    starter kit rather than this product

The second is a rebrand.sh defect worth reporting upstream. rebrand.sh:400
applies the DESCRIPTION argument to package.json alone, while
project.config.ts's projectDescription is what actually reaches
og:description and twitter:description. You pass a description and it
silently never reaches a user.

